{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1564621-diablerie-limit","id":1564621,"title":"Diablerie Limit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-10-08T18:46:23-07:00","id":1564621,"title":"Diablerie Limit","content":"I've got this character concept. So some Ordo Dracul is trying to create a super-vampire by means of Diablerie. So he picks out a promising young vampire and trains them up. They have a duel and whoever wins eats the other. The mentor usually wins, but the apprentice wins often enough to shake things up. How many times can this happen before the winner goes completely bugfuck?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28699-321rg","name":"321RG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-08T18:54:55-07:00","id":1564623,"title":"","content":"Sooner or later, a neonate will catch on and perhaps, bring his mentor a, <i>surprise duel</i> the Ordo Dracul wasn't expecting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-08T19:17:19-07:00","id":1564625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iguazu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1564621-diablerie-limit?p=1564623#post1564623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sooner or later, a neonate will catch on and perhaps, bring his mentor a, <i>surprise duel</i> the Ordo Dracul wasn't expecting.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's how the mentor won against his own master. What I'm asking about is how stable can this be? The master and apprentice chain is composed of vampires of different clans and masteries. So as to cover all the bases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28699-321rg","name":"321RG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-08T22:09:46-07:00","id":1564630,"title":"","content":"Until their luck runs out.<br /> <br /> VTR core p101, &quot;Diablerie is always a breaking point, regardless of the vampire\u2019s Humanity score.&quot;<br /> <br /> Theoretically they could just keep succeeding on their rolls but if they're just locked in a cage and let out only to kill they're going to be hitting a lot of Breaking Points. There's little to keep them in touch with their Humanity there. <br /> <br /> And with the Tainted Condition the victims can tamper with their luck until they're fully 'digested,' or just try to ensure their killer dies.<br /> <br /> If it doesn't happen, this vampire is eventually going to be stacked with Disciplines and Skills that may help them turn the tables on their captor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-09-2026, 01:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-08T23:23:47-07:00","id":1564631,"title":"","content":"This is definitely the kind of thing that is likely to lead to weird consequences that are not defined as consistent outcomes in the rules. There's no rule that says what happens when you eat a thousand souls, but that's not because the only bad thing that results from eating a thousand souls is the defined consequence for eating a soul, happening a thousand times. It's because this is a rare enough situation that it's more interesting to craft bespoke stories around it.<br /> <br /> Strange cursed bloodlines might emerge; this might even attract some kind of bizarre entity, like the <i>alu</i> to the En, or cause some kind of convergent adaptation with the nature of the strix. The devoured souls might battle for control from within or form a gestalt personality. The vampire might degenerate with heavy banes and feeding restrictions, like the consequences of thickening Blood Potency on overdrive. Or the vampire might just be a vampire, if one with uniquely supreme self-control and care to mind his detachment from Humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-09T11:22:15-07:00","id":1564644,"title":"","content":"The Coil of Ziva (Secrets of the Covenants) would help a lot with this.<br /> <br /> 2 Buttress the Soul<br /> When facing Detachment, she may spend Vitae, up to her normal per-turn limit. Every Vitae spent adds one die to resist Detachment. So Depending on BP you can add between 1 and 15 dice to your Detachment roll<br /> <br /> 3 Enliven the Anima<br /> Any time she\u2019d suffer a Condition for Detachment, you may choose to spend a Willpower point to take Raptured instead.<br /> <br /> Scale<br /> Bleed the Sin<br /> Reduce the subject\u2019s next Humanity trait purchase by one Experience per dot of the vampire\u2019s Coil of Ziva. Since humanity is 2 Experience per dot I'm guessing the author meant by one beat per dot of the vampire\u2019s Coil of Ziva.<br /> <br /> Siphon the Soul<br /> Lets you steal a point of humanity when doing Diablerie, it has a detachment roll (which you can boost with Buttress the Soul), meaning there are three outcomes:<br /> Fail both detachment rolls, Lose 1 Humanity.<br /> Fail one, pass one detachment roll, net 0 change Humanity stays the same.<br /> Pass both rolls, Diablerie actually increases humanity by 1 point. With 2+ dice on detachment you should gain Humanity faster than you lose it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Between boosted rolls, 1 xp humanity, and draining humanity, its fairly easy to get a humanity 10, BP 10 Diablerist.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Denying the Bane 1<br /> &quot;Add her Coil dots to her Humanity for the purpose of determining the effects of her Banes. This includes her clan Bane. If this increases her effective Humanity to 10, such Banes do not affect her. &quot;<br /> <br /> Embracing the Banes 4<br /> Your character can sustain a number of Banes equal to her Willpower dots, not three.<br /> So if you have ziva 5, and humanity 5+ you can have upto 10 banes that don't actually harm you in any way and let you ignore 10 different breaking points, further easing keeping a high humanity score.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/299-ninedaysdead","name":"NineDaysDead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-09T11:56:58-07:00","id":1564646,"title":"","content":"What kind of training are we talking, and how long is it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-09T12:56:40-07:00","id":1564649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1564621-diablerie-limit?p=1564646#post1564646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of training are we talking, and how long is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Each link in the chain is different. One mentor focuses on the mental Disciplines so his apprentice can focus on the physical ones. A few mentors fully expect to get eaten while others are fattening up the apprentice for their own gain.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28699-321rg","name":"321RG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-09T13:06:12-07:00","id":1564650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>321RG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1564621-diablerie-limit?p=1564649#post1564649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each link in the chain is different. One mentor focuses on the mental Disciplines so his apprentice can focus on the physical ones. A few mentors fully expect to get eaten while others are fattening up the apprentice for their own gain.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, the training isn't necessarily relevant to the duel?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-09T13:50:40-07:00","id":1564651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1564621-diablerie-limit?p=1564650#post1564650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, the training isn't necessarily relevant to the duel?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes, part of the training is how to deal with a superior foe. Then there's the fact that the training is meant to be well rounded and cover whatever situation the super-vamp would find themselves in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28699-321rg","name":"321RG","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-10-10T01:27:43-07:00","id":1564659,"title":"","content":"Michael's question is way too important for a simple answer, because it actually lies at the core of it all.<br /> <br /> No rule defines this beyond Detachment, but as Stupid Loserman said this is unique enough in a game defined by strangeness and unique situations leading to unique outcomes.<br /> <br /> But what will better inform what's an adequate answer or not is the process itself. How targets are selected and trained isn't incidental, it is the most important question. Or why they keep the experiment going.<br /> <br /> What they do to avoid the explicit problem of suffering Breaking Points? This is a game term and mechanic, but the phenomenon it models in the setting is known to the characters.<br /> <br /> Also what Coil they're in right now? What Scale is deemed necessary? How those relate, what's the theory? Is it a proposal for a new Coil? The Coil of Ziva may be useful, but may not be the best choice for the goal of the experiment.<br /> <br /> The idea is interesting. And if you want it to go sour royally, it's a sensible decision and indeed very probable outcome. It can go bad in too many ways. But it can also be a success to a degree and produce a new Coil, Bloodline or whatever. Even just a very powerful vampire.<br /> <br /> One way or another fleshing out the methods and people involved is the only way to answer what can happen that will be interesting and make some sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}